    <briefdescription>
<para>Multi-GPU work load balancer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Distributes GPU work requests across a list of available devices using configurable strategies. Tracks per-device allocation load and skips unhealthy devices automatically.</para>
<sect1 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1autotoc_md30_1s1"><sect2 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1autotoc_md30">
<title>Strategies</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>ROUND_ROBIN — select devices in sequence, skipping unhealthy ones.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>LEAST_LOADED — select the device with the most free VRAM.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>FIRST_HEALTHY — always select the first healthy device (deterministic, useful for single-GPU environments).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1autotoc_md31_1s1"><sect2 id="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1autotoc_md31">
<title>Integration with DeviceDiscovery</title><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1aa19f8191ecdcea6b2ab89353456db830" kindref="member">updateDevices()</ref></computeroutput> refreshes the device list from the discovery layer. <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1a6c7b5a07d77b31d4722cf2416f3e4977" kindref="member">markDeviceFailed()</ref></computeroutput> can be called when a runtime error is detected to remove a device from selection until <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_g_p_u_load_balancer_1a0abbb286d46ce53a920fbaef21754428" kindref="member">resetDevice()</ref></computeroutput> is called.</para>
<para>Thread safety: all public methods are protected by an internal mutex. </para>
</sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
